--TEST--
A `Core\Request::postAs` or `queryAs` conversion collects every field that did not fit into one `ParseError`, and a `name` the request never carried is refused rather than read as an empty set — `rule:core-classes/derive-reports-every-field` and `rule:errors/ambiguous-input-refused`
--GET--
page=x
--POST--
age=&name=ada
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Two ways to fail in one call: a value `as` refuses — the empty string, which
// is not an exact numeric literal — and a required key the form never carried.
// The report is one throw carrying both, because a form needs the list rather
// than the first item of it.
try {
    Core\Request::postAs<{age: int, city: string}>();
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (ParseError $bad) {
    echo "issues=", Core\Arr::count($bad->issues) as string, "\n";
    echo "  ", $bad->issues["0"]->path, ": ", $bad->issues["0"]->message, "\n";
    echo "  ", $bad->issues["1"]->path, ": ", $bad->issues["1"]->message, "\n";
}

// The same reading over a query string, and the same refusal: `page=x` is a
// parameter that arrived and does not convert, which is one failed field
// rather than a `0` this member invented.
try {
    Core\Request::queryAs<{page: uint}>();
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (ParseError $loose) {
    echo $loose->issues["0"]->path, ": ", $loose->issues["0"]->message, "\n";
}

// A `name` the query never carried reaches `null`, which is not a set of
// fields — refused as one under `rule:errors/ambiguous-input-refused`, rather
// than answered as a `T` whose every field happened to be absent.
try {
    Core\Request::queryAs<{page: uint}>({name: "filter"});
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (ParseError $missing) {
    echo "issues=", Core\Arr::count($missing->issues) as string, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
issues=2
  age: expected int, found a string
  city: required field missing
page: expected uint, found a string
issues=1
